summary:
Repair the guildhouse textures that came back wrong from Higgsfield, in place.

Seen in the first in-game render (2026-10-18):
- thin bright seam lines across some tiles (timber, plaster, roof slate) - in the albedo and in
  the normal map derived from it;
- `wall_stone` drawn as multicoloured bricks (the palette read as stone colours), `timber` green;
- `floor_planks` and `ceiling_boards` greyscale (a height panel taken for the colour);
- `interior_plaster` with its "smoke near the top" band repeating every tile.

Fixes: seam rows / columns are replaced by interpolating their neighbours; off-

Our own textures for the hero kit, generated from the meshes (numpy + Pillow, seeded, so every
run gives the same images). Nothing here copies pixels from the Quaternius textures; only the
meshes' UV layouts and geometry are used.

- `skin(body)`: base colour and normal map in the body's UV layout, baked from the mesh:
  * cavity / occlusion (how much nearby surface stands above a point's tangent plane) darkens and
    cools creases; convex points (curvature) catch light;
  * flushed zones near the cheeks, nose, ears, lips, knuckles, elbows and knees;
  * low-frequency mottling and fine pores;
